  "kind": "obds-word-boundary-ci-fixtures",
  "note": "Section 11.5 promised that word_boundary_ci is pinned by registry fixtures. No such fixture shipped in 2.0.0, so two implementations could not agree on the one mode whose meaning is delegated to a segmentation implementation. These are that fixture set: the normative contract is the declared Unicode version plus these cases. The declared version is the one the pinned segmentation engine implements, which is not section 14.3c's canonicalisation pin — those are two questions with two answers, and conflating them made the declaration false. An implementation that reproduces these cases agrees with the reference; one that does not, does not, whatever segmentation library it uses.",
